                <pb facs="0731" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10075: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-17T14:00:00+03:00">April 17, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 18—10:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>245. While the Government decided last evening that it would leave tonight, plans
                    are still only in the formative stage, shipping facilities <pb facs="0732"
                        n="720" xml:id="pg720"/> being apparently inadequate for official, private
                    and possibly military needs. Yugoslav Government is still here and more members
                    are expected today. Meanwhile the armies continue to fall back and rumors of
                    disorganization are rife. The Germans appear to have established complete air
                    superiority and reliable news from front is scanty and always delayed.</p>
                <p>Under these circumstances chances of a reasonably safe evacuation of Diplomatic
                    Corps appear slim and the Dean who is the Turkish Ambassador has already decided
                    for this reason to stay here whatever happens. I and my small staff are ready to
                    leave at a moment’s notice but am dependent on the Government for arrangements
                    and will not take undue risks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
